  "summary": "Full assessment of all 170 German/Vietnamese passages: five chapter headings and every paragraph, translated directly from the 1912 German text. The first reviews scored 8.55 (units 1–100) and 8.60 (101–170), with four majors (a pupa read as a puppet, a doffed cap misread, garbled syntax around the marble mass of language, and a wrong referent for ‘den Entbehrten’); one round of fixes and fresh separate-context blind reviews then scored 8.675 (units 1–100) and 8.73 (101–170) with no major open, and a last one-word consistency fix for ‘Der Elende’ closed the one remaining major. The final score is taken from the weakest range, 8.675 on the half-point scale, above the unchanged 8.6 threshold. A few minor points remain open.",
